/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  column03_azeotrope_mesh
  =======================

  Ethanol/water (NRTL) distillation by the rigorous SIMULTANEOUS (MESH
  Newton) method.  This is the payoff of the v0.48 solver: ethanol/water
  forms an azeotrope at x_eth ~ 0.894 (1 atm), and the sequential
  bubble-point (Wang-Henke) is unstable here -- on this very case it does
  NOT converge (200 outer iters).  The MESH Newton converges in ~5
  iterations to a PHYSICAL distillate (x_eth ~ 0.80, below the azeotrope).

  Feed: 100 kmol/h, 30/70 ethanol/water, 1 atm, a SATURATED LIQUID -- said
  once, by the stream: `phase liquid;` at the feed's own bubble point under
  this case's NRTL, 354.42 K (the engine's bubbleT on this stream gives
  354.4248 K; rounded DOWN so the feed's own equilibrium agrees with the
  pin).  Until 2026-10-05 the stream said T = 363 K and the column said
  `feedQuality 1.0`: at 363 K this feed is a VAPOUR (V/F = 1 by the
  engine's own flash), so the case said two different things.  The column
  priced a liquid, the energy report priced the vapour, and the plant
  boundary carried a 1149.69 kW residual -- the latent heat of the feed --
  that this header used to describe as closing.  The column now reads a
  feed by what it MEANS (DEV.md D1), so the contradiction refused, and the
  case was corrected to declare the saturated liquid it was designed
  around.  A vapour feed at 363 K is NOT a drop-in alternative: with
  q = 0 this specification (R = 2.5, D = 25 kmol/h) leaves the stripping
  section without vapour, which the MESH reports as a non-positive flow.
  Column: 16 stages, feed at 8, R = 2.5, D = 25 kmol/h, method simultaneous.

  Expected: converged; x_D(ethanol) ~ 0.80 (< 0.894 azeotrope -- physical);
  T_top ~ 351.4 K (the azeotropic temperature); mass closes 100%.

  NOTE: asking for a distillate ABOVE the azeotrope (x_eth > 0.894) is
  physically impossible -- no method converges, and that is correct.  The
  MESH method does not invent a non-physical "past the azeotrope" answer
  (which the bubble-point used to do).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       simultaneous;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( distillate  bottoms );

        operation
        {
            nStages        16;
            feedStage      8;
            refluxRatio    2.5;
            distillateRate 25.0 kmol/h;
            P              1.01325 bar;
        }
    }
);
